# Agents Gone Wild — Build Plan\par
\par
## 1) Show Positioning\par
\par
**Core promise:** Break down real AI-agent failures in a way that's useful, entertaining, and practical.\par
\par
**Audience:**\par
- Builders (PMs, engineers, founders)\par
- Operators (support, security, risk teams)\par
- Curious professionals who are AI-adjacent\par
\par
**Episode formula (repeatable):**\par
1. **The incident** (what happened)\par
2. **The root cause** (why it happened)\par
3. **The prevention** (what to do differently)\par
4. **The takeaway** (one-line lesson)\par
\par
Tagline idea: **"When agents go off script, we go under the hood."**\par
\par
---\par
\par
## 2) Content Pillars\par
\par
Use these to keep episodes varied but coherent:\par
\par
1. **Wrong Thing** — harm, policy breach, data leak, unauthorized action.\par
2. **Bad Thing** — business/legal/reputation damage from poor guardrails.\par
3. **Funny Thing** — harmless chaos, weird loops, prompt hijinks.\par
4. **Near Misses** — incidents that were caught early (great for prevention lessons).\par
\par
Create a weekly mix (example):\par
- 1 major breakdown episode\par
- 2 short clips from episode\par
- 1 carousel/text post with prevention checklist\par
- 1 “news break” quick reaction when relevant\par
\par
---\par
\par
## 3) Episode Formats for X and LinkedIn\par
\par
### A) Flagship Weekly Episode (6–12 minutes)\par
- Host on video platform (YouTube or native uploads).\par
- Publish teaser + thread on X.\par
- Publish native video + text summary on LinkedIn.\par
\par
### B) Shorts (30–90 seconds)\par
- "Incident in 60 seconds"\par
- "One mistake, one fix"\par
\par
### C) Thread/Carousel Breakdown\par
- Slide/Post 1: Headline incident\par
- Slide/Post 2: What failed\par
- Slide/Post 3: Why safeguards failed\par
- Slide/Post 4: Prevention checklist\par
- Slide/Post 5: Your opinion / CTA\par
\par
---\par
\par
## 4) Weekly Production Workflow (from scratch)\par
\par
### Monday — Research & Selection\par
- Monitor incidents from security blogs, model provider updates, AI/dev communities, X, LinkedIn.\par
- Score candidate incidents with this rubric (1–5 each):\par
  - Impact\par
  - Novelty\par
  - Evidence quality\par
  - Teachability\par
  - Virality potential\par
\par
### Tuesday — Script\par
- Build script in this structure:\par
  - Hook (15 sec)\par
  - Story timeline (90 sec)\par
  - Root-cause analysis (2–4 min)\par
  - Prevention framework (2–4 min)\par
  - CTA (15 sec)\par
\par
### Wednesday — Record\par
- Batch record flagship + 2 short clips.\par
- Capture clean A-roll plus 3–5 B-roll/screenshots.\par
\par
### Thursday — Edit and Package\par
- Edit long episode + shorts.\par
- Prepare captions/subtitles.\par
- Create thumbnail and title variants.\par
\par
### Friday — Publish & Engage\par
- Publish on X + LinkedIn.\par
- Respond to comments in first 60–90 minutes.\par
- Collect analytics after 24 hours.\par
\par
---\par
\par
## 5) Brand and Voice Guidelines\par
\par
**Voice:**\par
- Sharp, non-hysterical, evidence-based, slightly playful.\par
- Avoid fearmongering.\par
\par
**Principles:**\par
- Critique systems, not individuals.\par
- Separate verified facts from inference.\par
- Always include prevention guidance.\par
\par
**Visual identity starter:**\par
- Dark background + warning accent color.\par
- Repeating frame: "Incident → Cause → Prevention".\par
- Consistent lower-third and title card.\par
\par
---\par
\par
## 6) Operating Model and Tooling\par
\par
### Minimal Stack\par
- Research tracking: Notion/Airtable sheet\par
- Script writing: Google Docs/Notion\par
- Recording: Riverside/Zoom + local backup\par
- Editing: Descript/Premiere/CapCut\par
- Scheduling: Buffer/Hypefury/Taplio\par
- Analytics dashboard: simple spreadsheet weekly rollup\par
\par
### Incident Database Fields\par
- Incident name\par
- Date\par
- Source links\par
- Type (wrong/bad/funny/near miss)\par
- Affected system\par
- Observable failure\par
- Suspected root cause\par
- Guardrail failures\par
- Prevention controls\par
- Confidence level (high/med/low)\par
\par
